<Layout
	title="Garden Sun support — Peculiar Engineer"
	description="Requirements, common questions and contact details for the Garden Sun iPhone app."
	kind="page"
	showDate={false}
>
	<h2>What you need</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>An iPhone with ARKit</li>
		<li>iOS 17 or later</li>
		<li>Location and camera permission</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Common questions</h2>

	<h3>Why does the sun line look off?</h3>
	<p>Move away from metal and give the compass a moment.</p>

	<h3>Why do typical sun hours need the internet?</h3>
	<p>
		The estimate uses data from NASA POWER, which the app fetches over the internet. The reply is
		cached on your phone for 30 days.
	</p>

	<h3>What is the spot file for?</h3>
	<p>
		It's a copy of a spot's location and notes, for you to keep or send. The app can't import it
		yet, and plant choices are not in it.
	</p>

	<h3>How do I delete everything?</h3>
	<p>Delete the app. Spot files you exported stay where you put them, so delete those there.</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Email <a href="mailto:apps@peculiarengineer.com">apps@peculiarengineer.com</a>. I usually
		reply within a few days.
	</p>

	<hr />
